CLASS com/xk72/proxy/ssl/SSLHandshakeParser com/xk72/proxy/ssl/SSLHandshakeParser
	COMMENT reassembles handshake messages out of the record bodies MaybeSSLRecordListener hands it,
	COMMENT parses ClientHello (type 1), ServerHello (type 2) and Certificate (type 11), and calls
	COMMENT the protected hooks below. Every other subclass in this package exists to fill one or
	COMMENT two of those hooks in.
	FIELD field_3783 state Lcom/xk72/proxy/ssl/SSLHandshakeParser$State;
		COMMENT [charles4] Charles 4's mapping corpus also read this field as `state`.
	FIELD field_3784 messageType B
		COMMENT the first byte of the handshake message: 1 ClientHello, 2 ServerHello, 11 Certificate.
	FIELD field_3785 messageLength I
		COMMENT the 3-byte length that follows the type byte.
	FIELD field_3779 messageBody [B
	FIELD field_3781 messageBytesRead I
		COMMENT how much of messageBody is filled; a handshake message can span several records.
	FIELD field_3786 handshakeStartTime J
		COMMENT set from System.currentTimeMillis() in the constructor and subtracted at
		COMMENT change_cipher_spec to give the handshake duration. Charles 4's corpus called this
		COMMENT classInitTime, which does not fit an instance field assigned per parser.
	FIELD field_3780 durationReported Z
		COMMENT guards handshakeDuration so only the first change_cipher_spec reports it.
	FIELD field_3782 handshakeSize J
	FIELD field_4717 LOGGER Lorg/slf4j/Logger;
	METHOD method_3770 setClientHello (Lcom/xk72/proxy/ssl/class_1387;)V
		COMMENT [charles4] Charles 4's corpus named this setClientHello, which matches: it is called
		COMMENT with the parsed type-1 message.
		ARG 1 clientHello
	METHOD method_3175 setSslDetails (Lcom/xk72/proxy/ssl/class_1385;)V
		COMMENT [charles4] called with the parsed type-2 ServerHello.
		ARG 1 sslDetails
	METHOD method_3176 setServerCertificates (Ljava/util/List;)V
		COMMENT [charles4] called with the chain out of a type-11 Certificate message. Despite the
		COMMENT name the client-side subclasses use it for the client's own certificates.
		ARG 1 certificates
	METHOD method_3743 setHandshakeSize (J)V
		COMMENT [inferred] the running handshake byte total. Charles 4's corpus called it
		COMMENT setResponseHandshakeSize, but the request-side subclasses feed it to
		COMMENT ProxyEvent.setRequestHandshakeSize, so the direction does not belong in the name.
		ARG 1 totalBytes
	METHOD method_3744 setHandshakeDuration (J)V
		COMMENT [inferred] milliseconds from construction to the first change_cipher_spec; the
		COMMENT subclasses keep the larger of this and what the ProxyEvent already holds.
		ARG 1 millis
	METHOD method_3748 handshakeMessage (B[B)V
		COMMENT [inferred] one fully reassembled handshake message. A RuntimeException while parsing
		COMMENT is swallowed to a debug log, so a malformed hello degrades to missing detail rather
		COMMENT than a failed connection.
		ARG 1 messageType
		ARG 2 body
	METHOD method_3793 handshakeRecord ([B)V
		ARG 1 body
	METHOD method_3792 handshakeSizeChanged (J)V
		ARG 1 recordBytes
	METHOD method_3174 alert (BB)V
		ARG 1 level
		ARG 2 description
	METHOD method_3747 changeCipherSpec ()V
	METHOD method_3745 applicationData ()V
	METHOD method_3750 encryptedRecord ()V
	METHOD method_3749 unknownRecord ()V
	METHOD method_3746 notSslRecord ()V
